{"id":"reserve-ai-an-early-chatbot-fooled","date":"2026-11-20","topic":"ai","region":"americas","headline":"An Early Chatbot Fooled People into Sharing Secrets","source":{"name":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ELIZA"},"accent":"us","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"Joseph Weizenbaum made an early computer program at MIT.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The simple program turned human words into easy questions.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Many people felt the computer really understood their feelings.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","S","S","M","V","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"His secretary asked him to leave the private room.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"She wanted to talk to the machine alone.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":96,"core1800":2,"ngsl":0,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":2},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"made","title":"Past Simple Tense","note":"The simple past tense is used for completed actions in the past. Here, 'made' is the irregular past form of the verb 'make'."},{"i":3,"focus":"asked him to leave","title":"Verb + Object + Infinitive","note":"This structure is used when asking or ordering someone to do an action. 'Him' is the object, and 'to leave' specifies the action requested."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"A scientist at MIT built a simple chatting program named ELIZA.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","M","M","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"It turned user statements into questions, so people felt heard.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","M","M","M","S","V","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"Many users believed that the software understood their deep feelings.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","M","S","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Weizenbaum felt surprised because people quickly formed emotional attachments to it.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","C","M","S","M","V","O","O","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"His own secretary even asked him to leave his office.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","M","V","O","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"She wanted to have a private talk with the computer.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":85,"core1800":8,"ngsl":5,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":2},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"so people felt heard","title":"Conjunction So for Result","note":"The conjunction 'so' connects a cause to its result. It shows that turning statements into questions caused people to feel heard."},{"i":3,"focus":"felt surprised","title":"Linking Verb with Complement","note":"The verb 'felt' connects the subject 'Weizenbaum' to the adjective 'surprised'. The adjective describes his emotional state."}]},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"In 1966, an MIT professor named Joseph Weizenbaum created an early chatbot called ELIZA.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"A chatbot is a computer program that can converse with human users.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","C","C","C","S","V","V","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"ELIZA rephrased user statements into open questions to simulate a human therapist.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Although the program lacked real understanding, many users felt deeply connected to it.","voice":null,"roles":["M","S","S","V","O","O","S","S","V","M","C","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Users have shared very personal thoughts with the software since its creation.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Weizenbaum was surprised when his secretary asked him to leave the office.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","C","M","S","S","V","O","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"She wanted to have a private conversation with the program by herself.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":78,"core1800":10,"ngsl":2,"tsl":0,"nawl":1,"beyond":9},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"that can converse with human users","title":"Relative Clause with That","note":"The relative clause modifies 'a computer program'. The relative pronoun 'that' functions as the subject inside this descriptive clause."},{"i":4,"focus":"have shared","title":"Present Perfect Tense","note":"The present perfect tense 'have shared' connects past actions to the present. It shows that sharing thoughts began in the past and continues up to now."}]},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"During the 1960s, computer scientist Joseph Weizenbaum developed ELIZA at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","S","S","S","S","V","O","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The system was designed to test natural language processing, which allows computers to analyze human text.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","O","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"By running a script called DOCTOR, ELIZA mirrored user statements in the style of a psychotherapist.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Although the software possessed no genuine understanding, many users quickly formed strong emotional attachments to it.","voice":null,"roles":["M","S","S","V","O","O","O","S","S","M","V","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Weizenbaum reported that some users frequently forgot that they were conversing with a simple computer.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","S","S","M","V","M","S","V","V","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"He was particularly astonished when his secretary asked him to step out of the room.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","C","M","S","S","V","O","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"She insisted on holding a private conversation with the automated software without any observers present.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"This unexpected psychological reaction was later named the ELIZA effect by computer scientists.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","M","V","C","C","C","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":75,"core1800":12,"ngsl":5,"tsl":2,"nawl":1,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"was designed to test","title":"Passive Voice with Infinitive","note":"The passive form 'was designed' indicates that the system received the action. The infinitive 'to test' follows to explain the purpose of the system."},{"i":6,"focus":"insisted on holding","title":"Preposition Followed by Gerund","note":"Prepositions like 'on' must be followed by a noun or a gerund (-ing form). Here, 'holding' functions as the noun object of 'on'."}]},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"Created by Joseph Weizenbaum at MIT in 1966, ELIZA remains one of the earliest milestones in natural language processing software.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"Operating through a primitive pattern-matching system, the program analyzed input text and converted user statements into reflective questions.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","M","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"By mimicking the conversational style of a non-directive psychotherapist, the program generated an illusion of genuine human empathy and comprehension.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Despite Weizenbaum's explicit explanations that the software lacked true consciousness, users routinely shared their personal thoughts with the machine.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","M","V","O","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The creator was particularly astonished when his own secretary requested that he vacate his office during her computer interaction.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","M","C","M","S","S","S","V","M","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"She sought a private dialogue with the program, momentarily treating the cold computer code as a trustworthy listener.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Researchers later coined the phrase \"the ELIZA effect\" to describe how easily people attribute human emotion to automated tools.","voice":null,"roles":["S","M","V","O","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Decades after its creation, this classic experiment still highlights the surprising psychological connections between humans and early software.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","S","S","S","M","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":65,"core1800":13,"ngsl":9,"tsl":2,"nawl":4,"beyond":7},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"Created by Joseph Weizenbaum at MIT in 1966","title":"Past Participle Introductory Phrase","note":"This participle phrase modifies the main subject 'ELIZA'. It concisely provides background information equivalent to a passive clause."},{"i":4,"focus":"requested that he vacate","title":"Subjunctive Mood in That-Clause","note":"Verbs expressing requests or demands often take a 'that' clause with a base verb. Here, 'vacate' is used instead of 'vacated' because of the subjunctive structure."}]}},"glossary":[{"word":"attachments","lemma":"attachment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈtætʃmənts/","definition":"strong feelings of affection or connection to something","tiers":["t2","t4"]},{"word":"rephrased","lemma":"rephrase","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riːˈfreɪzd/","definition":"to express something in a different way","tiers":["t3"]},{"word":"simulate","lemma":"simulate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈsɪmjəleɪt/","defini